---
import { reuseTrace } from './first-copy-model.mjs';
interface Props { kind: 'journey' | 'reuse' | 'cost' | 'freshness' }
const { kind } = Astro.props;
const titles = {journey:'Follow one request',reuse:'The same traffic, different reuse',cost:'The price of a shortcut',freshness:'Two copies, one change'};
---
<figure class="cache-figure" data-first-copy={kind} aria-label={titles[kind]}>
 <span class="figure-title">{titles[kind]}</span>
 {kind === 'journey' && <>
  <div class="controls" role="group" aria-label="Initial cache state"><button data-warm="false" aria-pressed="true">First request · empty cache</button><button data-warm="true" aria-pressed="false">Later request · copy present</button></div>
  <svg viewBox="0 0 480 335" role="img" aria-label="A reader sends a request to the application. The application checks Redis, and on a miss reads the catalogue and saves a copy.">
   <path class="wire" d="M65 170H240L420 70M240 170L420 270" />
   <path class="wire active-wire" data-route d="M65 170H240" />
   <rect class="node" x="10" y="127" width="110" height="86" rx="8"/><text x="65" y="152" text-anchor="middle">Reader</text><text class="value" data-reader x="65" y="188" text-anchor="middle">?</text>
   <rect class="node" x="185" y="127" width="110" height="86" rx="8"/><text x="240" y="152" text-anchor="middle">Application</text><text class="value" data-app x="240" y="188" text-anchor="middle">—</text>
   <rect class="node" data-cache-box x="365" y="27" width="110" height="86" rx="8"/><text x="420" y="52" text-anchor="middle">Redis</text><text class="value" data-cache x="420" y="88" text-anchor="middle">empty</text>
   <rect class="node" x="365" y="227" width="110" height="86" rx="8"/><text x="420" y="252" text-anchor="middle">Catalogue</text><text class="value" x="420" y="288" text-anchor="middle">€18</text>
   <text class="small" x="240" y="238" text-anchor="middle">Chooses the path</text>
   <circle class="parcel" data-parcel cx="65" cy="170" r="7" />
  </svg>
  <div class="controls"><button data-play>Play request</button><label class="scrubber">Progress <input data-progress aria-label="Request progress" type="range" min="0" max="1000" value="0" step="1" /></label><button data-reset>Reset</button></div>
  <p class="readout" data-status aria-live="polite">1 / 8 · Ask for the mug.</p>
  <figcaption>The moving dot is a message. On a miss the application queries the catalogue, builds an answer, stores a copy and replies. On a hit it replies from the copy. Message travel is slowed for visibility; this is a sequential model, not a timing measurement.</figcaption>
 </>}
 {kind === 'reuse' && <>
  <div class="controls"><label>Different products <input data-distinct aria-label="Number of different products" type="range" min="1" max="24" value="4" /><output data-distinct-value>4</output></label></div>
  <div class="request-grid" aria-label="Twenty-four requests in arrival order">{reuseTrace(4).map((r,i) => <div class="request-cell" data-cell={i}><b>#{r.key}</b><small>waiting</small></div>)}</div>
  <div class="controls"><button data-play>Play requests</button><label class="scrubber">Requests <input data-progress aria-label="Requests completed" type="range" min="0" max="24" step="1" value="0" /></label><button data-reset>Reset</button></div>
  <p class="readout" data-status aria-live="polite">0 requests · 0 catalogue reads · 0 hits.</p>
  <figcaption>Read left to right, then down. A numbered box asks for that product. The first request builds a copy; later requests reuse it. This model keeps every copy and has no updates, expiry, eviction or overlapping requests.</figcaption>
 </>}
 {kind === 'cost' && <>
  <div class="controls"><label>Hits in 100 requests <input data-hits aria-label="Hits in 100 requests" type="range" min="0" max="100" value="90" /><output data-hits-value>90</output></label></div>
  <div class="controls"><label>Build answer from source <input data-source aria-label="Source path duration in milliseconds" type="range" min="1" max="80" value="20" /><output data-source-value>20 ms</output></label></div>
  <div class="bar-row"><span>Without cache</span><div class="bar-track"><i class="bar source" data-direct-bar style="width:83.333%"></i></div><output data-direct>20 ms</output></div>
  <div class="bar-row"><span>Cache hit</span><div class="bar-track"><i class="bar lookup" data-hit-bar style="width:8.333%"></i></div><output>2 ms</output></div>
  <div class="bar-row"><span>Cache miss</span><div class="bar-track"><i class="bar lookup" data-lookup-bar style="width:8.333%"></i><i class="bar source" data-source-bar style="width:83.333%"></i><i class="bar fill" data-fill-bar style="width:8.333%"></i></div><output data-miss>24 ms</output></div>
  <div class="bar-row"><span>Average</span><div class="bar-track"><i class="bar lookup" data-average-lookup style="width:8.333%"></i><i class="bar source" data-average-source style="width:8.333%"></i><i class="bar fill" data-average-fill style="width:0.833%"></i></div><output data-average>4.2 ms</output></div>
  <div class="legend"><span><i class="lookup"></i>Lookup</span><span><i class="source"></i>Read + assemble</span><span><i class="fill"></i>Save copy</span></div>
  <p class="mean" data-mean>4.2 ms average with the cache</p>
  <p class="readout" data-status aria-live="polite">10 catalogue reads instead of 100. Each miss takes 24 ms.</p>
  <figcaption>Invented durations, including network travel: lookup 2 ms, fill 2 ms. Requests wait for the fill. The bars share one scale, which changes with source duration. There are no queues, failures or variation within either path.</figcaption>
 </>}
 {kind === 'freshness' && <>
  <svg viewBox="0 0 480 285" role="img" aria-label="The catalogue changes from 18 to 15 euros at five seconds. Its cached copy remains 18 euros until it expires at ten seconds, unless it is invalidated.">
   <rect class="node" x="40" y="15" width="160" height="100" rx="8"/><text x="120" y="42" text-anchor="middle">Catalogue</text><text class="value" data-source-price x="120" y="80" text-anchor="middle">€18</text>
   <rect class="node cached" data-copy-box x="280" y="15" width="160" height="100" rx="8"/><text x="360" y="42" text-anchor="middle">Cached answer</text><text class="value" data-copy-price x="360" y="80" text-anchor="middle">€18</text>
   <text data-copy-label x="240" y="153" text-anchor="middle">Both copies agree</text>
   <path class="wire" d="M40 205H440"/><path class="wire" d="M40 196V214M207 196V214M373 196V214M440 196V214"/>
   <text class="small" x="40" y="238" text-anchor="middle">0s</text><text class="small" x="207" y="238" text-anchor="middle">5s</text><text class="small" x="373" y="238" text-anchor="middle">10s</text><text class="small" x="440" y="238" text-anchor="middle">12s</text>
   <text class="small" x="40" y="261" text-anchor="middle">Fill</text><text class="small" x="207" y="261" text-anchor="middle">Change source</text><text class="small" x="373" y="261" text-anchor="middle">Expiry</text>
   <circle class="parcel" data-clock cx="40" cy="205" r="7"/>
  </svg>
  <div class="controls"><button data-play>Play time</button><label class="scrubber">Time <input data-progress aria-label="Time in seconds" type="range" min="0" max="12" step="0.1" value="0" /></label><output data-time>0.0 s</output><button data-reset>Reset</button></div>
  <div class="controls"><label><input data-invalidate type="checkbox" /> Delete the copy when the source changes</label></div>
  <p class="readout" data-status aria-live="polite">The copy has 10.0 seconds left. No further requests have arrived.</p>
  <figcaption>The source changes at 5 seconds; the copy's ten-second lifetime starts at its fill. Deleting or expiring the copy does not delete the source or fetch a replacement. Here the write and optional deletion are instantaneous; later articles open the gap between them.</figcaption>
 </>}
 <noscript><p>Enable JavaScript to operate the illustration. The diagram and caption show the initial state and describe the mechanism.</p></noscript>
</figure>
<script>
 import './first-copy.js';
</script>
